Weakness confirmed and root cause understood. The `iss` validator lacks `array: true`, but the verify loop still coerces array values and passes if **any** element matches the allowlist. So `iss: ["https://evil-iss", "https://valid-iss"]` is accepted though it carries a disallowed issuer — which a strict RFC 7519 verifier (iss = single StringOrURI, must equal the trusted issuer) rejects.

